From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maago <maago@example.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 03:04:23 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Edit a post

Change a post: its author and staff, its title and body.

- Two routes and two views:

      maago.GET("/posts/{id}/edit", "post_edit", EditPost),
      maago.POST("/posts/{id}/edit", "post_change", ChangePost),

      func EditPost(ctx context.Context, u auth.User, db maago.DB, in EditPostIn) (PostEditPage, error)
      func ChangePost(ctx context.Context, u auth.User, tx maago.Tx, in ChangePostIn) (maago.Result[PostEditPage], error)

  After its route, the POST view would be UpdatePost, but maago
  generates UpdatePost for Post. Name views clear of the generated GetX,
  InsertX, UpdateX and DeleteX (as RemovePost in 0023)
- Both ask editable(ctx, db, u, id): a hidden post is a 404, anybody
  else gets a 403 on GET too (mayChange, 0022)
- The form PostEditForm takes Title and Body from model=Post. When to
  pin and publish is decided when the post is written: changing them
  here would need the pin check to leave the post itself out, and a
  schedule already past would fail Validate's "in the past" check
- EditPost fills the form's Raw with the post's values. The template
  always draws Raw
- The same-title check asks PostTitleTaken again. So that the post being
  changed does not count, it gets an optional parameter skip_id? and a
  line {skip_id} AND id <> :skip_id (like q? in search_posts.sql). A
  new post's SkipID is nil, and the line drops out: savePost stays as
  it is
- Two people with the form open at once: the later save must not undo
  the earlier one unseen. The form's action carries the version the
  post had when the form opened, its UpdatedAt in microseconds:

      <form method="post" action="{{url "post_change" .Post.ID}}?version={{.Version}}">

  ChangePostIn reads it (Version int64 `maago:"query=version"`; a POST
  without it is a 400), and ChangePost hands it to UpdatePost as the
  version to write over:

      changed.UpdatedAt = time.UnixMicro(in.Version)

  UpdatePost returns maago.ErrConflict when the post has another version
  by now. ChangePost then shows the form again, with what was written
  and an error on the form; it keeps the old version, so it saves only
  once opened anew. The version rides in the URL because a model form's
  fields are the model's
- The save is UpdatePost, which writes the whole row and moves
  UpdatedAt. Only the title and body of the post read are changed, so
  the other columns stay
- A link to edit on the post page

The table gets post_edit and post_change: as publishing, its author
or staff. post_change's URL carries the version, and a change moves
it, so ann and staff each change a post of their own. TestEdit sees
that the post's own title and the same title on another board pass and
another post's title on this board does not; that a form opened before
a save saves nothing; and that the pin and schedule times stay.

